{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473971-dominate-presence-question","id":1473971,"title":"Dominate/Presence question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-04T07:14:58-08:00","id":1473971,"title":"Dominate/Presence question","content":"Are lupines immune to Dominate and Presence when in Crinos form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T07:27:40-08:00","id":1473972,"title":"","content":"Lupines, as in the not-necessarily Garou antagonists of VtM? No.<br /> <br /> Garou in WtA? Neither.<br /> <br /> Eye-Contact, which is necessary for Dominate, might be tricky, Though. But unless the Garou has a specific Gift or other power to help him (or Merit) normal rules apply. The Glabro, Crinos or Hispo Form don't provide any benefits here.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Vampire wouldn't use Dominate/Presence on a wolf, normally, but I'd rule a garou in lupus form would be affected, but not by Animalism. That's just my feeling, no crossover rules consulted...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T10:05:50-08:00","id":1473980,"title":"","content":"Good to know. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T12:26:31-08:00","id":1473991,"title":"","content":"VtM has been fairly consistent that Animalism (at least below levels that deal with things like Frenzies) works on &quot;normal&quot; animals, and not on supernaturals that are in animal forms, and the reverse to thing like Dominate.<br /> <br /> The big danger of using Presence specifically on a Garou in Crinos is that extreme emotions are Frenzy triggers (and most vampires don't know the specifics there), and Crinos makes it easier to Frenzy. So it's not immunity, but there are really good reasons to not use powers willy-nilly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-06T01:39:26-08:00","id":1474069,"title":"","content":"Which would let us circle back to the question, if Frenzy makes immune to Dominate/Presence.<br /> <br /> There was once a sidebar in some VtM book, stating the difficulty of dominate is increased by 2, if subject is in frenzy (and eye contact is even more difficult).<br /> <br /> And while an emotion, like fear, probably is not affecting a Frenzy, Presence 2 is a supernatural power that has a specific result if activated successfully. Should Frenzy, a more or less mundane thing, me stronger than a supernatural power, or not?<br /> The rules of Frenzy and Powers are formulated as absolutes, not taking into account how they interact but only how they change the behaviour of a person unaffected by anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-06T14:10:51-08:00","id":1474092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473971-dominate-presence-question?p=1474069#post1474069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which would let us circle back to the question, if Frenzy makes immune to Dominate/Presence.<br /> <br /> There was once a sidebar in some VtM book, stating the difficulty of dominate is increased by 2, if subject is in frenzy (and eye contact is even more difficult).<br /> <br /> And while an emotion, like fear, probably is not affecting a Frenzy, Presence 2 is a supernatural power that has a specific result if activated successfully. Should Frenzy, a more or less mundane thing, me stronger than a supernatural power, or not?<br /> The rules of Frenzy and Powers are formulated as absolutes, not taking into account how they interact but only how they change the behaviour of a person unaffected by anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frenzy is &quot;mundane&quot; and a liability for vampires. For werewolves, there's a stat track that measures the magnitude of fury (Rage), and both merits and Gifts that are either more effective in a frenzy or require it to work, such as Mars Midsky or Mad Strength. Even though both games refer to them with the same word, they might not be the exact same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-06T23:53:05-08:00","id":1474110,"title":"","content":"My house rule allows rolling Rage to resist mind-control powers (of course, must know you are being controlled first). I think it\u2019s ok","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T21:09:01-08:00","id":1474159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473971-dominate-presence-question?p=1474069#post1474069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And while an emotion, like fear, probably is not affecting a Frenzy, Presence 2 is a supernatural power that has a specific result if activated successfully. Should Frenzy, a more or less mundane thing, me stronger than a supernatural power, or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Presence 2 would send a Frenzying werewolf into a Fox Frenzy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T01:55:01-08:00","id":1474176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473971-dominate-presence-question?p=1474159#post1474159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Presence 2 would send a Frenzying werewolf into a Fox Frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but then would Fox Frenzy rules apply and the duration would depend on the trigger's presence (is the trigger the fear emotion or the vampire?) and Willpower rolls, not the successes of the Presence roll....<br /> <br /> In my experience it is most balanced if one sticks to the rules presented by the power.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}